"PDCL","gene_symbol_current":"PDCL","gene_id":"ENSG00000136940","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.000127078,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.13805,"nucleus_score":-3.98137,"pct_ad":0.105202,"pct_control":0.114421,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.802076,"donor_log2fc":-0.121773,"donor_lfcse":0.098794,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.0132683}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000136940","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0296793,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.680759,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000136940","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0446413,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000136940","entrez_id":["5082"],"uniprot":["Q13371"],"ncbi_summary":"Phosducin-like protein is a putative modulator of heterotrimeric G proteins. The protein shares extensive amino acid sequence homology with phosducin, a phosphoprotein expressed in retina and pineal gland. Both phosducin-like protein and phosphoducin have been shown to regulate G-protein signaling by binding to the beta-gamma subunits of G proteins. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q13371","text":"Acts as a positive regulator of hedgehog signaling and regulates ciliary function. [Isoform 1]: Functions as a co-chaperone for CCT in the assembly of heterotrimeric G protein complexes, facilitates the assembly of both Gbeta-Ggamma and RGS-Gbeta5 heterodimers. [Isoform 2]: Acts as a negative regulator of heterotrimeric G proteins assembly by trapping the preloaded G beta subunits inside the CCT chaperonin."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}